GCExpression _ BracketRing -- Substituting top-degree Grassmann-Cayley elements into the bracket ring
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note _: (Macaulay2Doc)_us,
  * Usage: 
        a = b_R;
  * Inputs:
      * b, an instance of the type *note GCExpression: GCExpression,, 
      * R, an instance of the type *note BracketRing: BracketRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a, an instance of the type *note GCExpression: GCExpression,, 

Description
===========

Interpreting bracket polynomials as functions on $\Lambda^d (V)$ (see *note
GCExpression ^ GCExpression: GCExpression ^ GCExpression, for notation), we may
convert an extensor $a_1 \wedge \cdots \wedge a_d$ to the bracket $[a_1, \ldots
, a_d].$

